        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T22:45:03Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can disable fields present in GKI for production kernels. In such case drivers which were compiled with GKI kernel and passed compliance test will be broken when switching to production kernel.\n\nBesides we don\u0027t have many memcgs and when CONFIG_MEMCG is disabled we have none, so the overhead of this should be tiny.\n\nI need to check what are the GKI requirements for Android Go devices. Maybe it makes sense to have a different ABI for them since CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE and most likely some other features are not needed there.",
      "parentUuid": "7975b909_db346dd5",
      "revId": "2318165502fb53fd6c24159006a13b5e2ac81fd2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "854d633f_b949c5e3",
        "filename": "include/linux/memcontrol.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 335,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T23:32:36Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Suren, Pratik is thinking about non-GKI uses of the android11-5.4 kernel (like Go devices or other small memory devices). I think it does make sense to wrap these new elements in something. Maybe instead of removing CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE, change it to something like:\n\n  #if defined(CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE) || defined(CONFIG_GKI_HUGEPAGE_FIELDS)\n\nAnd then define GKI_HUGEPAGE_FIELDS in gki_defconfig. Clearly no-one else would define this so non-GKI small-memory devices wouldn\u0027t incur the memory overhead.",
      "parentUuid": "4aab8cba_d3d6e4da",
      "revId": "2318165502fb53fd6c24159006a13b5e2ac81fd2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a09824d_06f3c41e",
        "filename": "include/linux/memcontrol.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 335,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-30T00:21:13Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Ok, now I get it. Will replace with #if defined(CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE) || defined(CONFIG_GKI_OPTIONAL_FEATURES) and will define CONFIG_GKI_OPTIONAL_FEATURES only inside gki_defconfig. This will enable these fields unconditionally in GKI but not in non-GKI kernels.",
      "parentUuid": "854d633f_b949c5e3",
      "revId": "2318165502fb53fd6c24159006a13b5e2ac81fd2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
